{"type": "message", "id": "6789bf00", "parentId": "3beb5470", "timestamp": "2026-04-07T05:00:39.254Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_JMGiklnvzI2mTgrIznDonFwN", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"site:nationsreportcard.gov Arizona 2022 grade 8 mathematics average score 274\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 908,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a3c844468c4a9c7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9a3c844468c4a9c7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"61db4271a1fc84e3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points. The average score decline for public schools in the nation decreased by 5 points. To view score changes for fourth-grade public school students in mathematics between 2022 and previous assessment years, or between other combinations of assessment years, use the drop-down menu to select a comparison year.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"61db4271a1fc84e3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"956ba8ea3fb775a7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: State Student Group Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"956ba8ea3fb775a7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/groups/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a2ddf3f18f953f4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWhile average scores decreased between 2019 and 2022 for almost all student groups nationally, this overall pattern differed across the states. Compared to 2019, female students scored lower in 38 states in 2022, whereas male fourth-graders scored lower in 26 states.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0a2ddf3f18f953f4\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"48b969d1c90b492d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Mathematics: National Average Scores\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"48b969d1c90b492d\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/nation/scores/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"708809ef7dcebfa3\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP reports scores at five selected percentiles to show the progress made by lower- (10th and 25th percentiles), middle- (50th percentile), and higher- (75th and 90th percentiles) performing students. In comparison to 2019, the 2022 mathematics scores were lower for fourth-grade students at all five selected percentiles.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"708809ef7dcebfa3\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9f63c8866931fbf4\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExplore Results for the 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9f63c8866931fbf4\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/?grade=8\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"199d752b041e5d3b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDownload a summary of the 2022 mathematics results. ... More detailed mathematics assessment results are available throughout this Report Card. ... The NAEP mathematics assessment measures students&#x27; knowledge and skills in mathematics and students&#x27; ability to apply their knowledge in problem-solving situations. The NAEP mathematics assessment framework specifies the mathematical content assessed at grades 4, 8, and 12.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"199d752b041e5d3b\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1a97399488e79ddd\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP Report Card: 2022 NAEP Mathematics Assessment\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1a97399488e79ddd\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/highlights/mathematics/2022/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ffdcdb6c61a0b4d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn 2022, fourth- and eighth-grade mathematics scores declined for most states/jurisdictions as well as for most participating urban districts compared to 2019. <strong>Average scores are reported on NAEP mathematics scales at grades 4 and 8 that range from 0 to 500</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9ffdcdb6c61a0b4d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.nationsreportcard.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "site:nationsreportcard.gov Arizona 2022 grade 8 mathematics average score 274", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 908, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a3c844468c4a9c7\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNAEP Mathematics: State Average Scores\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9a3c844468c4a9c7\">>>", "url": "https://www.nationsreportcard.gov/mathematics/states/scores/?grade=8", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"61db4271a1fc84e3\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn the 43 states/jurisdictions where scores were lower in 2022 than 2019, the size of the score differences ranged from 2 to 14 points. The average score decline for public sc